WEBVTT

NOTE whisper small.en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.560
One of the most fun and exciting applications of confidence recently has been neural style transfer.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.440
You get to implement this yourself and generate your own artwork in the programming exercise.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.440
But what is neural style transfer? Let me show you a few examples.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:24.000
Let's say you take this image. This is actually taken from Stanford University, not far from my Stanford office.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.920
And you want this picture recreated in the style of this image on the right.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.840
This is actually a Van Gogh's starry night painting.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.360
What neural style transfer allows you to do is generate a new image like the one below,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:48.680
which is a picture of the Stanford University campus, but painted, but drawn in the style of the image on the right.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:57.080
In order to describe how you can implement this yourself, I'm going to use C to denote the content image,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:03.040
S to denote the style image, and G to denote the image you will generate.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.960
Here's another example. Let's say you have this content image.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.840
So that C, this is of the Golden Gate Bridge in San Francisco.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.720
And you have this style image. This is actually a Pablo Picasso image.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:26.880
You can then combine these to generate this image G, which is the Golden Gate painted in the style of that Picasso shown on the right.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.320
The examples shown on this slide were generated by Justin Johnson.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:37.400
And what you learn in the next few videos is how you can generate these images yourself.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:45.040
In order to implement neural style transfer, you need to look at the features extracted by ConfNet at various layers,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.800
the shallow and the deeper layers of a ConfNet.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.920
So before diving into how you can implement neural style transfer,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:59.840
what I want to do in the next video is try to give you better intuition about what are all these layers of a ConfNet really computing.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.080
Let's take a look at that in the next video.
